+    """#1314: is this literal argument a network URL rather than a path? A scheme other than
+    `file:` (`http://127.0.0.1:8760/health`), or, as the argument of a URL client, `host:port[/…]`
+    (`curl localhost:8760/health`). A `..` component disqualifies it: if a directory named `http:`
+    existed, `http://../x` would be a real escape. (Whether such a directory exists is checked
